<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28351" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕdĭtāmentum</span></b> ,
			i, n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				thinking of</i> any thing, <i>a preparation</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">belli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					4, 26</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. A. 15, 35</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arietum meditamenta,</span>”
				<i>thoughtfully prepared battering-rams</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 4, 10</span></i>
			.— *</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic.; plur.: puerilia, <i>rudiments</i> taught to children at school, <i><span class="en">Gell. 8, 10</span></i>
			<i>in lemm</i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
